# Heartwood Crafter: "{T}: Add {C}. This mana can't be spent to cast spells from your hand" (CR 106.6, 601.2a). Turn 1 it
# enters prepared (CR 722.3a), Soul Tether's copy in exile. Turn 3 its {C} beside the untapped Forest can't make a Mind
# Stone from the hand ({2}: the {C} can't pay for it, the Forest's {G} alone is one short) - the refusal; then, with a
# Mountain played, the {C}, the Forest's {G} and the Mountain's {R} pay for Soul Tether's copy cast from exile (CR 722.3c),
# which is not the hand: the pool is empty after, the Crafter unprepared and a Heartwood token made, which taps for {R}
# or {G}. Turn 5 the Forest and Mountain cast the Mind Stone from the hand, and the Crafter's {C} pays the {1} of the
# Mind Stone's ability - an ability, not a spell from the hand - which draws a card.

